                      </div>\r\n                      </div>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n                                <!-- <div class=\"booking-section\" data-section=\"5\">\r\n                  <div class=\"container mobile-only-break-768\">\r\n                    <div class=\"booking-section-content\">\r\n                      <div class=\"section-title font-blue font-uppercase font-small  font-title\">Checkout</div>\r\n\r\n                      <button class=\"button button-blue booking-next-step t\" data-action=\"6\">Checkout</button>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                </div> -->\r\n\r\n                    </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n\r\n        </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"template-bottom\">\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"template-bottom-inner\">\r\n          <div class=\"template-bottom-mobile\">\r\n\r\n\r\n            \r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"template-left\">\r\n\r\n                          <h2 class=\"template-subtitle font-bold font-xsmall\">FROM THE DIRECTOR OF THE OSCAR-WINNING ALL QUIET ON THE WESTERN FRONT</h2>\r\n                                      <div class=\"te\">\r\n    <p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Nominated for 8 Oscars for the 2025 ceremony including Best Picture.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i>\"An entertainingly juicy adaptation of Robert Harris’s novel\" <strong>Guardian ★ ★ ★ ★</strong></i></p><p>The Pope has died. Cardinal Lawrence must lead the Conclave to select the new leader of the Catholic world. But as high-ranking cardinals gather, he discovers sides have been drawn and secrets that might destroy a future pope, perhaps even the Church itself, threaten to be revealed. Following his Oscar-winning success with All Quiet on the Western Front, <strong>Edward Berger </strong>presents us with another tale of conflict, albeit one where battles are waged in hushed tones in hallowed hallways.<strong> Fiennes</strong>, <strong>Tucci </strong>and <strong>John Lithgow</strong> make the most of <strong>Peter Straughan’s</strong> (Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy) screenplay, based on<strong> Robert Harris</strong>’ 2016 novel, with <strong>Isabella Rossellini </strong>making a cameo as the formidable Sister Agnes.</p></div>            \r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"template-right\">\r\n              \r\n                        <div class=\"event-details\">\r\n\r\n\r\n                            <div class=\"event-detail-section event-info\">\r\n\r\n                <div class=\"rating-info font-tag font-uppercase font-title font-blue \">Rating Information: </div>\r\n\r\n                <div class=\"event-info-text age-rating text\"><span>brief sexual violence references</span></div>\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n                                          <div class=\"event-detail-section event-info\">\r\n                <div class=\"rating-info font-tag font-uppercase font-title font-blue \">Run time:</div>\r\n                <div class=\"event-info-text\"><span>120 mins</span></div>\r\n              </div>\r\n\r\n              \r\n              \r\n              \r\n                              <div class=\"event-detail-section event-info\">\r\n                  <div class=\"rating-info font-tag font-uppercase font-title font-blue \">Year of release:</div>\r\n                  <div class=\"event-info-text\"><span>2024</span></div>\r\n                </div>\r\n\r\n              \r\n                              <div class=\"event-detail-section event-info\">\r\n                  <div class=\"rating-info font-tag font-uppercase font-title font-blue \">Company:</div>\r\n                  <div class=\"event-info-text\"><span>Black Bear</span></div>\r\n                </div>\r\n              \r\n                              <div class=\"event-detail-section event-info\">\r\n                 