          "bodySize": 13299,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "size": 13299,
            "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n\n<!--[if lt IE 7]>\n<html lang=\"en\"\n      class=\"no-js ie legacy-ie lt-ie10 lt-ie9 lte-ie9 lt-ie8 lt-ie7\"> <![endif]-->\n<!--[if IE 7]>\n<html lang=\"en\"\n      class=\"no-js ie legacy-ie lt-ie10 lt-ie9 lte-ie9 lt-ie8\"> <![endif]-->\n<!--[if IE 8]>\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"no-js ie legacy-ie lt-ie10 lt-ie9 lte-ie9\"> <![endif]-->\n<!--[if IE 9]>\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"no-js ie legacy-ie lt-ie10\"> <![endif]-->\n<!--[if gt IE 9]><!-->\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"no-js\"> <!--<![endif]-->\n<!--[if !IE]><!--><script>if(document.documentMode) document.documentElement.className+=' ie'+document.documentMode;</script><!--<![endif]-->\n\n<head>\n\n            <script>(function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':\n                new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],\n                j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src=\n                'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);\n          })\n                              (window, document, 'script', 'dataLayer', 'GTM-W5VLL9M');\n                  </script>\n    \n    <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=Edge,chrome=1\">\n<title>London Breeze Preview: The End + Q&A with George Mackay\r\n | Riverside Studios</title>\n\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"London Breeze is thrilled that award-winning actor, George MacKay (1917, Femme, Captain Fantastic) will join us for a Q&amp;A following a special preview screening of The End from Academy Award®-nominated director Joshua Oppenheimer (The Act of Killing, \">\n    \n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"London Breeze Preview: The End + Q&A with George Mackay\r\n | Riverside Studios\">\n<meta name=\"generator\" content=\"Grandad Digital - Powered by You.Create Content Management System\">\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n  \"url\": \"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/\",\n  \"logo\": \"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/assets/img/logo.png\"\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"London Breeze Preview: The End + Q&A with George Mackay\",\"description\":\"London Breeze is thrilled that award-winning actor, George MacKay (1917, Femme, Captain Fantastic) will join us for a Q&amp;A following a special preview screening of The End from Academy Award\\u00ae-nominated director Joshua Oppenheimer (The Act of Killing, The Look of Silence) in partnership with MUBI and Riverside Studios. The End is a poignant and deeply human musical about a family that survived the end of the world. It is also Oppenheimer\\u2019s debut feature drama following his highly successful documentaries.Twenty-five years after environmental collapse left the Earth uninhabitable, Mother (Tilda Swinton), Father (Michael Shannon) and Son (George MacKay) are confined to their palatial bunker, where they struggle to maintain hope and a sense of normalcy by clinging to the rituals of daily life\\u2014until the arrival of a stranger, Girl (Moses Ingram), upends their happy routine. Son, a na\\u00efve twenty-something who has never seen the outside world, is fascinated by the newcomer, and suddenly the delicate bonds of blind optimism that have held this wealthy clan together begin to fray. As tensions rise, their seemingly idyllic existence starts to crumble, with long-repressed feelings of remorse and resentment threatening to destroy the family\\u2019s delicate balance. But their reckoning with difficult truths also points to a different way forward, one based on acceptance, love, and a capacity for change.An urgent and unforgettable cautionary tale, The End stars Academy Award\\u00ae winner Tilda Swinton (Michael Clayton), Academy Award\\u00ae nominee Michael Shannon (Nocturnal Animals, Revolutionary Road), George MacKay and Moses Ingram (Lady in the Lake, The Queen\\u2019s Gambit). The screenplay is by Oppenheimer and Rasmus Heisterberg (A Royal Affair), with songs by Joshua Schmidt (music) and Oppenheimer (lyrics).\",\"image\":[\"https:\\/\\/riversidestudios.co.uk\\/images\\/uploads\\/361b60a4dcd1eecc0d2963c015c7d885.jpeg\"],\"startDate\":\"2025-03-21T18:00:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2025-03-21T18:00:00+00:00\",\"eventStatus\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\\/EventScheduled\"}</script>\n<link rel=\"shortcut icon\" href=\"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/assets/favicons/favicon.ico?1651755466\" />\n    <link href=\"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/see-and-do/london-breeze-preview-the-end-qa-with-george-mackay-163948/\" rel=\"canonical\"/>\n\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=5, user-scalable=yes\"/>\n<link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/\"/>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"//code.jquery.com/ui/1.12.1/themes/base/jquery-ui.css\">\n<!-- <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/daterangepicker/daterangepicker.css\" /> -->\n\n<link href=\"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/assets/css/styles.min.css?v=b660f5e1efcf1b00290891e9f653159e\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" />\n<script>\n  document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className.replace(/\\bno-js\\b/, 'js');\n  var base_url = 'https://riversidestudios.co.uk/',\n    gdrck = '6LffRNoZAAAAAJIWWC7QG27lobOmUg6S4sE9GI8k',\n  gdmaps = {},\n    $ajaxRequestSent = false;\n</script>\n\n    <script>\n      var gdEvents = false;\n    </script>\n    \n\n            <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"/>\n                        <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"London Breeze Preview: The End + Q&A with George Mackay - Riverside Studios\"/>\n                        <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://riversidestudios.co.uk/see-and-do/london-breeze-preview-the-end-qa-with-george-mackay-163